===Etymology===
The {{glossary|adverb}} is a terser form of {{m|en|ex. gr.}}, both {{glossary|abbreviation|abbreviating}} {{der|en|la|exemplī grātiā|t=for the sake of an example}};<ref>{{cite-book|author=[[w:John Traupman|John C[harles] Traupman]]|title=The New College Latin and English Dictionary|edition=3rd|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher={{w|Bantam Books}}|year=2007|isbn=978-0-553-59012-8}}.</ref> ''e.g.'' was also used as an abbreviation in Latin.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=adv|id=6994550712|date=January 2018}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=abbrev}}</ref>

The {{glossary|noun}} is derived from the adverb.

